<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Uí Dúnlainge</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Uí Dúnlainge were a dynasty of north Leinster, in the plains of modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kildare">Kildare</a>, descended from Dúnlaing mac Énda Niada. From the 8th to the 11th century they held the kingship of Leinster almost without break, rotating it between three branches, the Uí Muiredaig, Uí Fáeláin and Uí Dúnchada, and controlled the monastery of Kildare. Their rivals were the Uí Chennselaig of south Leinster, who regained power in the 11th century.</p></div>
